520 - He Hideth My Soul
 / 
Key: C
Time: 4/4
Tempo: Moderato
Number: 520
Topic: Christian Life - 

Verse 1:
[C]A wonderful Savior is [F]Jesus my [C]Lord,
A wonderful Savior to [G]me,
He [C]hideth my soul in the [F]cleft of the rock,
Where [C]rivers of [G]pleasure I [C]see.
He [G7]hideth my soul in the [C]cleft of [F]the [C]rock
That [G]shadows a dry, thirsty [C]land;
He hideth my life in the [F]depths of His love,
And [C]covers me [G]there with [G7]His [C]ha[Bdim]nd, [C]
[F]And [C]covers me [G7]there with His [C]hand.

Refrain:
[C]He hideth my [F]soul in the [C]cleft of the rock
[G]That shadows a dry, thirsty land;
[C]he hideth my life in [F]the depths of His love,
[C]And covers [G]me there [C]with His hand,
[G7]And [C]covers me [F]there with [C]His hand.

Verse 2:
[C]A wonderful [F]Savior is [C]Jesus my Lord,
[G]He taketh my burden away,
[C]He holdeth me up, and [F]I shall not be moved,
[C]He giveth [G]me strength [C]as my day.

Verse 3:
[C]With numberless [F]blessings each [C]moment He crowns,
[G]And filled with His fullness divine,
[C]I sing in my [F]rapture, Oh, Glory to God
[C]For such [G]a Redeemer [C]as mine.

Verse 4:
[C]When clothed [F]in His brightness, [C]transported I rise
[G]To meet Him in clouds of the sky,
[C]His perfect salvation, [F]His wonderful love,
[C]I'll shout [G]with the [C]millions on high.
